- Layout of one node, as the four decisions a flex box actually takes: which way
- the children go, how they line up across and along it, how far apart they are,
- and whether this node stretches inside its own parent. Plus the width of the
- page, which is the same kind of fact and is what an artboard is set by.
-
- Every one of them is a key of the ordinary `style` dictionary of the node, so
- what this panel writes is what a hand written $mol document would carry, and an
- export needs to know nothing about artboards at all.
- @see ../../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 8
